Quresh, great to hear you're still working on this.

Yes, I think you've diagnosed the problem correctly.  I'll add one caveat, that I'm not entirely certain how the exporting of logdens.gamma - since it's a nimbleFunction, rather than a standard R object or function - will work.  It may work fine, but I'm not certain of that.  In the event that simply including logdens.gamma in your clusterExport (lines 26-27) doesn't play nicely with the exporting mechanism, then a very easy workaround is just to define the logdens.gamma nimbleFunction right inside your parallelization function, for example right after loading the nimble package, on line 39 of your function, before you create the model object or anything else.  I think that would work just fine.

Cheers,
